<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank puts cash machines in petrol stations.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank puts cash machines in petrol stations.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerzbank AG, Germany's third-largest commercial bank, said on Wednesday it would install automatic cash dispensers in petrol station shops run by Deutsche Shell AG throughout Germany.</p>
<p>Commerzbank said it would at first fit machines in 150 around-the-clock stations and has plans to install more later on.</p>
<p>The bank has tested the use of dispensers at three petrol stations in Frankfurt, Neu-Ulm and Hanover.</p>
<p>The move is part of a drive by German banks to woo customers by becoming easier to access. Banks have set up telephone banking subsidiaries and are now opened their branches longer and setting up branches in supermarkets.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
